<title>USA: Fannie Mae ups the size of REMIC 1997-26.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae ups the size of REMIC 1997-26.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae on Monday said it has increased the size of a previously issued series of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities.</p>
<p>REMIC trust 1997-26, issued via Greenwich Capital Markets, Inc, was increased by $435 million to $1.635 billion, the agency said. The issue is backed by various pools of 6.0 percent, 7.0 percent and 8.0 percent mortgage-backed certificates and various Fannie Mae REMIC tranches.</p>
<p>The issue has a settlement date of April 30, Fannie Mae said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
